    command: cd /home/j1/OrionsBelt && git commit -m "j1: bf16/fp16 recurrent-state variants of GDN kernels (ob-8qt.4)

Add four mixed-precision kernel variants to gdn_sve.c:
  gdn_cumdecay_bf16/f16 — narrow-format output, fp32 accumulator
  gdn_gated_scan_bf16/f16 — narrow-format persistent state, fp32 accumulator

CRITICAL CONSTRAINT honored: the decay/scan accumulator stays fp32
throughout. Only the storage format narrows. A decay product of 0.5^64
(~5e-20) underflows both bf16 and fp16, so the accumulator MUST be fp32.

Conversion strategy:
  bf16: software round-to-nearest-even (no ISA dependency)
  fp16: __fp16 cast → single FCVT instruction (base A64 ISA, works on A57)
  NEON: 4-lane vectorized conversion helpers for both formats

Correctness (test_gdn_mixed.c, ALL TESTS PASSED):
  bf16 state:  0.382% max relative error
