    command: cd /home/j1/OrionsBelt && bd remember "Session 3 (ob-8qt.4): Added bf16/fp16 state variants of gdn_cumdecay and gdn_gated_scan. Key findings: (1) bf16 state has 0.38% max relative error, fp16 has 0.05% — both within tolerance. (2) bf16 NEVER flushes to zero because it shares fp32's 8-bit exponent range — even 0.5^64 is representable. fp16 flushes for small decay products because its 5-bit exponent tops out at ±65504. (3) At seq=64 (prefill chunk), narrowing state has negligible bandwidth impact because state is ~1% of total traffic. The benefit is concentrated at decode (seq=1) where state is ~40% of traffic. (4) cumdecay_f16 is 34% faster than fp32 cumdecay on A57 because vcvt_f16_f32 (FCVTN instruction) is a single-cycle hardware op on base A64. (5) __fp16 scalar type and FCVTN/FCVTL vector conversions work on Cortex-A57 (Armv8.0-A) despite __ARM_FEATURE_FP16_VECTOR_ARITHMETIC not being defined — those macros gate fp16 ARITHMETIC (fmul/fadd on half regs), not conversion. Dolt merge conflict required --force push; teammate data from pull-at-session-start preserved." 2>&1

