○ ob-dqu · CPU optimization: big.LITTLE affinity policy and i8mm/SVE GEMM paths   [● P1 · OPEN]
Type: task
Created: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02

DESCRIPTION

  Exploit the asymmetric 4+4+4 cluster layout: pin latency-critical prefill to
  the A720 big cores, keep housekeeping on the A520 little cores, and avoid   
  cross-cluster migration mid-inference. Enable i8mm and SVE paths and verify 
  they are active at runtime. Fully Arm-specific and, unlike the NPU path, not
  gated on any external approval.                                             



NOTES

  UNBLOCKED FOR REAL WORK by ADR 0005: the RK3588 board has an asymmetric A76 
  big + A55 little layout, directly analogous to the O6's A720 big/medium +   
  A520 little. big.LITTLE affinity policy is now developable and MEASURABLE on
  hardware in hand rather than speculative. Use taskset to pin clusters; the  
  core-tuned binaries bench_gdn_rk3588_a76 and bench_gdn_rk3588_a55 exist for 
  exactly this comparison.                                                    



