NOTES

  WORKFLOW WRITTEN AND LOCALLY VERIFIED, BUT NOT ACTIVE - needs the           
  maintainer. This agent session pushes over an OAuth app without 'workflow'  
  scope, so GitHub rejects any push that creates .github/workflows/*:         
  'refusing to allow an OAuth App to create or update workflow ... without    
  workflow scope'. That restriction is deliberate (it stops an app silently   
  introducing CI that executes code), so rather than work around it the file  
  is parked at ci/github-workflow-ci.yml with ci/README.md explaining         
  activation.                                                                 
                                                                              
  TO ACTIVATE (maintainer, from a clone with normal credentials): git mv      
  ci/github-workflow-ci.yml .github/workflows/ci.yml && commit && push.       
                                                                              
  Four jobs, all commands verified locally: lint (ruff check + format), test  
  (pytest on 3.10 and 3.13), kernels (cross-compile + QEMU verification of all
  seven SVE1/SVE2/NEON/scalar targets via scripts/verify_cpu_kernels.sh),     
  onnx-probes (regenerate probes, assert onnx.checker + onnxruntime           
  execution). Deliberately does NOT run cixparse/cixbuild - the CIX SDK is a  
  licensed 461MB download that cannot be fetched in CI.                       
                                                                              
