### Key finding this session

The refreshed 28-row CSV revealed that **state narrowing is a prefill-only optimization**. At decode (seq=1), the GDN scan touches only ~80 KiB — entirely L2-resident — so fp32↔half conversion instructions cost more than the I/O savings. This is a concrete, measured argument: the mixed-precision headline should say "halves resident state during prefill," not "speeds up GDN."

